{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345440",
      "title": "Alternative Ways of Passing & Receiving / Handling \"props\"",
      "sourceHash": "24112db405e22522fb2f379a587d2ac83133630849be3d04c71e281a805b8155",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.653,
          "end": 5.402,
          "en": "So props are a crucial React concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.402,
          "end": 8.39,
          "en": "Components would not be very useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.39,
          "end": 12.395,
          "en": "if they weren't configurable with help of props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.395,
          "end": 15.248,
          "en": "And therefore, when working with React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.248,
          "end": 17.253,
          "en": "and when writing React code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.253,
          "end": 20.388,
          "en": "you will often set props on components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.388,
          "end": 23.988,
          "en": "and accept props as input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.988,
          "end": 26.67,
          "en": "Now, there are two things I wanna mention here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.67,
          "end": 29.497,
          "en": "two alternative ways of accepting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.497,
          "end": 32.755,
          "en": "or setting props you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.755,
          "end": 34.507,
          "en": "And I'll start with an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.507,
          "end": 37.277,
          "en": "of setting props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.277,
          "end": 39.74,
          "en": "because the use case we have here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.74,
          "end": 41.769,
          "en": "where we have a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.769,
          "end": 44.491,
          "en": "that needs almost all the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.491,
          "end": 47.141,
          "en": "we are working with in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.141,
          "end": 48.878,
          "en": "so that needs almost all fields",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.878,
          "end": 50.633,
          "en": "of that raw data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.633,
          "end": 53.623,
          "en": "That use case is quite common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.623,
          "end": 56.244,
          "en": "And you can then absolutely set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.244,
          "end": 59.616,
          "en": "multiple prop key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.616,
          "end": 62.512,
          "en": "So define multiple props of different names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.512,
          "end": 66.76,
          "en": "and pass your different values through those props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.76,
          "end": 70.265,
          "en": "But an alternative would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.265,
          "end": 73.148,
          "en": "to instead create an expense item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.148,
          "end": 75.731,
          "en": "where you just pass one prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.731,
          "end": 78.64699999999999,
          "en": "that could be titled expense, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.64699999999999,
          "end": 81.523,
          "en": "though the name as you learned is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.523,
          "end": 84.78,
          "en": "And instead of passing the individual values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.78,
          "end": 86.014,
          "en": "through multiple props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 86.014,
          "end": 89.518,
          "en": "you could then pass the entire data point.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.518,
          "end": 91.24,
          "en": "So the entire object in this array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.24,
          "end": 94.87700000000001,
          "en": "in this case here as one single prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.87700000000001,
          "end": 97.38900000000001,
          "en": "So as a value for one single prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 97.38900000000001,
          "end": 99.75999999999999,
          "en": "the expense prop in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.75999999999999,
          "end": 102.003,
          "en": "two expense item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.003,
          "end": 103.747,
          "en": "You could do that as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 103.747,
          "end": 107.632,
          "en": "instead of passing those individual props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.632,
          "end": 110.378,
          "en": "If you would use this approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 110.378,
          "end": 112.251,
          "en": "where you pass one single prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.251,
          "end": 114.378,
          "en": "instead of multiple props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.378,
          "end": 116.493,
          "en": "you, of course, also would have to change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.493,
          "end": 119.519,
          "en": "the code inside of the component because now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.519,
          "end": 122.646,
          "en": "you no longer get the title as a prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.646,
          "end": 125.256,
          "en": "Instead, you only get the expense prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.256,
          "end": 128.499,
          "en": "or whichever name you chose for the prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.499,
          "end": 130.901,
          "en": "So then here in the receiving component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 130.901,
          "end": 135.03,
          "en": "you would have to write props.expense.title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.03,
          "end": 139.143,
          "en": "props.expense.date and props.expense.amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 140.249,
          "end": 141.507,
          "en": "And of course, now, we would have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 141.507,
          "end": 144.239,
          "en": "to migrate all expense items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 144.239,
          "end": 146.381,
          "en": "to this alternative way of passing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 146.381,
          "end": 148.753,
          "en": "to the expense item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 148.753,
          "end": 150.38,
          "en": "Now, I wanna emphasize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 150.38,
          "end": 153.5,
          "en": "that both approaches are fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 153.5,
          "end": 155.005,
          "en": "You can pass a single prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 155.005,
          "end": 157.006,
          "en": "which contains the entire object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 157.006,
          "end": 158.274,
          "en": "or a multiple props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 158.274,
          "end": 160.996,
          "en": "which contain the individual values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 160.996,
          "end": 162.50900000000001,
          "en": "This is entirely up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.50900000000001,
          "end": 164.385,
          "en": "because it's your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 164.385,
          "end": 165.755,
          "en": "but I definitely wanted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 165.755,
          "end": 168.383,
          "en": "to mention this alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 168.383,
          "end": 170.984,
          "en": "With that, I'll delete this example though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 170.984,
          "end": 172.508,
          "en": "and switch back to the approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 172.508,
          "end": 173.89,
          "en": "I showed you before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 173.89,
          "end": 175.88400000000001,
          "en": "because I think it's a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 175.88400000000001,
          "end": 177.394,
          "en": "to understand and read,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 177.394,
          "end": 180.66,
          "en": "especially when you're just getting started with React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 182.497,
          "en": "But you could also pass everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 182.497,
          "end": 185.487,
          "en": "in one data object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 185.487,
          "end": 186.63,
          "en": "When working with props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 186.63,
          "end": 189.39,
          "en": "both approaches are fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 190.415,
          "en": "So with that, I'm of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 190.415,
          "end": 192.77100000000002,
          "en": "also updating expense item again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 192.77100000000002,
          "end": 196.382,
          "en": "and I'm moving back to the individual props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 196.382,
          "end": 199.137,
          "en": "Another alternative syntax you could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 199.137,
          "end": 201.632,
          "en": "when working with props is exclusive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 201.632,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "to the receiving component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 206.508,
          "en": "There, we're getting this props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 206.508,
          "end": 209.74,
          "en": "where we're then accessing the different properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 209.74,
          "end": 213.006,
          "en": "In this case, date, title, and amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 213.006,
          "end": 214.747,
          "en": "Instead of using this approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 214.747,
          "end": 218.7,
          "en": "we could also use a feature built-in to JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 221.625,
          "en": "and use object destructuring right here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 221.625,
          "end": 223.745,
          "en": "in the parameter list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 223.745,
          "end": 224.737,
          "en": "This might look strange",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 224.737,
          "end": 227.749,
          "en": "but it's regular JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 227.749,
          "end": 231.149,
          "en": "You can use the object destructuring syntax here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 231.149,
          "end": 232.249,
          "en": "where you add opening",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 232.249,
          "end": 235.007,
          "en": "and closing curly braces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 235.007,
          "end": 236.39,
          "en": "and where you then refer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 236.39,
          "end": 238.263,
          "en": "to the different properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 238.263,
          "end": 240.894,
          "en": "of the object you are receiving here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 240.894,
          "end": 243.894,
          "en": "so of the props object in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 243.894,
          "end": 248.24099999999999,
          "en": "to pull these values, buy those keys here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 248.24099999999999,
          "end": 250.381,
          "en": "out of that incoming object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 250.381,
          "end": 253.74099999999999,
          "en": "and store them in locally available variables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 253.74099999999999,
          "end": 257.253,
          "en": "of these titles, of these names here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 258.506,
          "end": 260.737,
          "en": "With that, the date prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 260.737,
          "end": 262.874,
          "en": "would be accessed with just date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 262.874,
          "end": 265.502,
          "en": "since we're pulling it out here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 265.502,
          "end": 267.741,
          "en": "Title would be accessed under just title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 267.741,
          "end": 271.379,
          "en": "and amount would be accessed under just amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 271.379,
          "end": 274.24,
          "en": "So here, we're using object destructuring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 274.24,
          "end": 277.126,
          "en": "This is not some special React syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 277.126,
          "end": 278.993,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 278.993,
          "end": 282.162,
          "en": "Instead, it's standard JavaScript syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 282.162,
          "end": 284.73199999999997,
          "en": "for using object destructuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 284.73199999999997,
          "end": 287.989,
          "en": "right in the function parameter list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 287.989,
          "end": 290.5,
          "en": "Now, again, I will actually switch back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 290.5,
          "end": 294.03,
          "en": "to the old approach which we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 294.03,
          "end": 296.67,
          "en": "where we instead use the .notation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 299.04,
          "en": "for accessing the different properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 299.04,
          "end": 301.138,
          "en": "But I wanted to share this alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 301.138,
          "end": 302.512,
          "en": "since you'll also see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 302.512,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "in many React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 307.803,
          "en": "and since you personally also might prefer it.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}